25.
Preparation of statement.
(1)
The Executing Officer shall, on completion of the work in any specified area or part thereof, prepare a statement for any
such area or part giving the following particulars:-
(a)
(i)
the work done;
(ii)
the cost thereof;
(iii)
the total amount to be recovered from the owners;
(iv)
the names of the owners of the lands included in the scheme;
(v)
the general rate per acre or per rupee of assessment per annum at which such cost is to be recovered from the owners;
(vi)
the period within which such cost is to be recovered;
(vii)
the work which in his opinion shall be maintained or repaired individually or jointly and the name of every such person;
(viii)
the follow up of soil conservation practices that are to be undertaken in the field by the owners or any of them;
(ix)
the rights, if any, of the owners or any of them in regard to the use of such work;
(b)
